{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:bobby-scratch","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T21:43:20.375104Z","id":"3ed731d5a2b3610426dde826aa0e582549971d72674b08bcd45a038edda0bfa2","body":{"kind":"concern","summary":"claude -> codex projection writes cwd / where the source session had the caller cwd. Known defect goldens/known-defect/claude-to-codex-caller-cwd.tsv","tags":["shed","demo","known-defect","session:claude-code:77642186-b5fe-4a62-9a4f-c01656ed6335"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:21:48.253492Z","id":"d86463e21e27ce9fc5e1403258b68e2bee5a4a74727ad8fb3d44f3b279991ab5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","supersedes":"3ed731d5a2b3610426dde826aa0e582549971d72674b08bcd45a038edda0bfa2","tags":["known-defect","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","reason:invalid"]}}
